{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.quantum_peter_weyl","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.quantum_peter_weyl","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Shared.SobolevHkRegularity"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.quantum_peter_weyl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.quantum_peter_weyl","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/quantum_peter_weyl.lean#L29-L41","doc":"**Content statement** (from manuscript):\n\nThe [spectral-Sobolev theory](#prop:q-spectral-sobolev) identifies\na single gap: completeness of the $\\Delta_q$-eigenbasis.  This\ntheorem closes it by proving the quantum Peter--Weyl theorem for\n$\\mathrm{SU}_q(2)$ using the categorical infrastructure already\navailable.\n\n    The Lean encoding below states the manuscript claim over a context class and discharges it from the class's fields (§3b-conditional). The declaration type-checks as a complete term; the substantive mathematical content is carried by the context-class axioms, and a full derivation from substrate primitives remains pending. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:quantum-peter-weyl","label":"thm:quantum-peter-weyl","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/quantum-peter-weyl.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QuantumPeterWeylContext.impl_quantum_peter_weyl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QuantumPeterWeylContext.impl_quantum_peter_weyl","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/quantum_peter_weyl.lean#L27-L27","doc":"Manuscript identity: `dim(V_j) = 2j + 1`, i.e. for `n = 2j`,\n`dim_V n = n + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QuantumPeterWeylContext.peter_weyl_active","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QuantumPeterWeylContext.peter_weyl_active","kind":"theorem","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/quantum_peter_weyl.lean#L24-L24","doc":"Hypothesis that Peter-Weyl holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QuantumPeterWeylContext.peter_weyl_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QuantumPeterWeylContext.peter_weyl_holds","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/quantum_peter_weyl.lean#L22-L22","doc":"Proposition: the quantum Peter-Weyl theorem holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QuantumPeterWeylContext.dim_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QuantumPeterWeylContext.dim_V","kind":"def","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/quantum_peter_weyl.lean#L20-L20","doc":"Categorical dimension `dim(V_j)` of the spin-`j` irrep, with\n`j` indexed by `n = 2j ∈ ℕ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QuantumPeterWeylContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QuantumPeterWeylContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/quantum_peter_weyl.lean#L17-L17","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QuantumPeterWeylContext.toSobolevHkRegularityContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QuantumPeterWeylContext.toSobolevHkRegularityContext","kind":"def","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41be